  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(0.85)=58.211\\,669\u2026\u2248{58.2117}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSince ${58.2117}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={58.2117}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={58.2117}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={58.2117}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/assets/ec4366c4e46cc9c1df5fb31aa2ca04f337fd3c6d0bce034405ca2b48874aa32a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}-{58.2117}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u2248{121.7883}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248{58.2}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248{121.8}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
